+# Local OpenAI-compatible API for split-LES inference (experimental)
+
+Run from the Mac with the matching `llama.cpp-omni` `llama-cli` and split GGUF weights:
+
+```bash
+python3 tools/les-openai-bridge/server.py --host 127.0.0.1 --port 18792 \
+  --bank 128 --ubatch 16 --depth 0 --context 4096
+```
+
+Routes: `GET /health`, `GET /v1/models`, `POST /v1/chat/completions` (nonstreaming). Supports a restricted OpenAI-style `tools` request with one model-generated function call or final answer per turn. Host executes tools; **server never executes tool calls**. Only loopback is permitted. Runtime model weights and binary arguments default to `/Volumes/ssd/les-eval/` and may be overridden.
+
+**Limitations:** every chat completion launches a fresh `llama-cli` process and rebuilds its KV state from the request's message transcript; no prompt cache, batching or streaming. Usage tokens are reported as zero because this prototype does not instrument the tokenizer; clients must not use them for accounting. CLI-generated tool calls are best-effort prompt-format JSON (not a fine-tuned function calling protocol). No multimodal request body is supported. This is intended for validation only, not deployment as a network API.
+
+```bash
+python3 -m unittest discover -s tools/les-openai-bridge -p 'test_*.py'
+curl --noproxy '*' http://127.0.0.1:18792/health
+```
+
+The adapter accepts both `{"tool":"replace_text","arguments":{"path":"source.py",...}}`
+and a model-produced flat format `{"tool":"replace_text","path":"source.py",...}`. It validates
+argument names and required fields before forwarding the OpenAI-style tool call.
+
+Local reproducibility experiment: `/Volumes/ssd/les-eval/agent-bench/real_tool_loop.py`.
+It can run only `run_tests`, `read_file`, and `replace_text` on disposable copies of
+`tasks/{session,stock,intervals}`. Every edit is restricted to `source.py`.
